    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜というより: rather than",
     "texto": [
      "To give the more exact description by comparing two ideas: **この りょうり は りょうり という より、 げいじゅつ です** (this food is more art than cooking).",
      "It's used when the first idea is almost true, but the second is fairer."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜というのは: the reason is that",
     "texto": [
      "In this use it introduces the reason for what was said: **わたし は にほんご を ならって います。 というのは、 しごと で にほんご が ひつよう だから です** (I'm studying Japanese because I need it for work). It can also introduce the definition of a word; context makes the use clear."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
